menu "USB Host Tab5 Example Configuration"

    config USB_HOST_TAB5_ROOT_PORT_POWER_ON_DELAY_MS
        int "Delay between host install and root-port power-on (ms)"
        range 0 5000
        default 500
        help
            A device attached at power-up is enumerated as soon as the root port
            powers on; this margin lets the board's supply settle after a cold
            boot before that first enumeration. 0 powers the port at once.

    config USB_HOST_TAB5_CONTROL_USB_A_POWER
        bool "Switch the USB-A jack's 5 V from the example"
        default y
        help
            The Tab5 switches the jack's 5 V through an IO expander, not the USB
            controller, so the host library's own root-port power-off does not
            reach a device on the jack. With this on, the jack is off from
            start-up until the host is listening, so a device attached at boot
            sees VBUS and a listening host together.

endmenu
